#
# Counter-example for the reasoned-graph math: expression-identity gate
# (crates/logic/src/math_expression.rs, check_structural_key_drift): ex:e1 is a
# well-formed math:NumberLiteral root, but its authored math:structuralKey is an
# obviously wrong string that cannot equal the recomputed blake3 digest of its own
# structure. The gate MUST raise math:StructuralKeyDrift (and neither of its two
# siblings math:SurfaceLeakInNormalForm / math:StructuralKeyOnRejectedExpression).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:e1 a math:NumberLiteral ;
    math:literalValue 1 ;
    math:structuralKey "not-the-real-digest" .
